Z||000000||Fret Naught||07-10-2000||12:52 PM||||I took advantage of the nice weather yesterday, and followed Orief's waxing routine on my car. I just had the hood painted about 6 weeks ago. I think I am going to have to learn how to paint, cause I sure found a myriad of flaws on my rig. I was sort of discouraged, I spent 500.00 on the hood alone, and when I got done yesterday, I could see deep buffing swirls, I could see some bodywork through the paint, I guess I am just too picky. So I got to thinking, just how hard is Base Coat Clear Coat to apply? I have painted acrlic enamel in the past, had a hard time with runs and sags, guys at work say heck you can do BC CC no problem its a piece of cake. What do you guys say? Or am I just too anal about this?||||reg||5
Z||000001||webbee||07-10-2000||05:02 PM||||If you paid $500.00 for hood paint and you can see body work through the paint I would take it back. Painting is a skill that is practice. Going slow is the key. Lots of thin coats is the best. You can somtimes pull a run off with a piece of masking tape that is as long as the run. Practice with spray cans and a handel to learn the "spray on" while moving movement. This is hard to explain on a chat line. Try to find a painter to show you. It's trial and error but can be mastered. Good luck!<p>[This message has been edited by webbee (edited 07-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||TOM||07-10-2000||09:41 PM||||bc/cc's are to bad to paint. I am used to spraying Imron which is a pain to get right.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Pretender||07-11-2000||12:47 AM||||imron is what my employer uses to paint the cranes and manlifts, it is very acceptible to orange peel, I would still go with a basecoat/clear. I guess it's mostly all to do with the painter and his experiance, electrostatic would be idel but since our cars are plastic thats not an option I also agree with Webbee, take it back and show them the inprofections. they should fix it free of charge. $500 is alot of money just for a hood, what else did you have done?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fret Naught||07-11-2000||12:55 AM||||Well, that was it just the hood, it was a custom paint that needed to be matched, lots of pearl and metal flake, and the match is real good.||||reg||1
